  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math>The reaction between CO of syn gas and steam in presence of catalyst is called water gas shift reaction.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>This reaction increases the yield of hydrogen obtained from coal gasification reaction as shown below.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#10230;</mo><munder><munder><mrow><mi>CO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&#9183;</mo></munder><mrow><mi>syn</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gas</mi></mrow></munder></math></p>",
